---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Auto-Billing 101" description="Learn how auto-billing and token billing work with Invoice Ninja's recurring invoicing and payment gateway integrations." path="/auto-billing-101/">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-50 to-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">Auto-Billing 101</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Everything you need to know about automatic billing for recurring invoices.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What is auto-billing for recurring invoicing? -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-dark mb-6">What is auto-billing for recurring invoicing?</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        If you have clients that need to be billed on a regular basis (daily, weekly, monthly, etc&hellip;), then you know exactly how time consuming this can be! First, you have to keep their credit card or bank details on file. Next, you must remember the date of the upcoming invoice. And then, you have to manually invoice the client. Every single time. All this on top of your regular work schedule and invoicing tasks.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
        If this spells &lsquo;hassle&rsquo; to you, Invoice Ninja comes to the rescue with token billing support via the world&rsquo;s favorite payment gateways:
      </p>

      <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-3 mb-8">
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Stripe
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Braintree
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Authorize.net
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Mollie
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          GoCardless
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Square
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Eway Rapid
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          PayFast
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Checkout.com
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Paytrace
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-primary flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
          Forte
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What is token billing? -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-dark mb-6">What is token billing?</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        Token billing is a feature that enables the payments system to capture your clients' credit card details and store them securely for billing at a future date. In short, token billing is what allows auto-billing, which means future recurring invoice payments can be processed automatically.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why would I need to auto-bill? -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-dark mb-6">Why would I need to auto-bill?</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        Perhaps you handle gigs on a regular basis for a particular client. It could be daily, weekly, monthly, or another frequency. Or maybe you have subscribers, who you need to bill every month, every six months&hellip; or even annually.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        Whatever the frequency and whatever the reason, token billing via Invoice Ninja provides the ultimate auto-billing solution for fixed recurring payments. Simply define the recurring invoice details, sit back, and let the token billing feature do the hard work for you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-gray-50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">Start Invoicing Today!</h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">Create. Send. Get Paid.</p>
      <Button href="https://app.invoicing.co/#/register" size="lg">Test Drive!</Button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
